<figure>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="bd-t bd-d" class="fig-dark" style="background:#131736">
    <title id="bd-t">How a bearing is measured</title>
    <desc id="bd-d">A compass circle centered on point A. A line points straight up to north. A second line runs from A to point B at the lower right. A curved arrow sweeps clockwise from north to the line to B, labelled 120 degrees. The same direction in quadrant form is south 60 degrees east, measured from south toward east.</desc>
    <circle cx="200" cy="170" r="125" fill="#1a2050" stroke="#3a4390" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <path d="M200 170 V 40" stroke="#aab0dc" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 6" />
    <path d="M200 170 V 300" stroke="#3a4390" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 6" />
    <path d="M200 170 L 308 232" stroke="#ff5fb4" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round" />
    <path d="M200 100 A 70 70 0 0 1 260.6 205" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#bd-arrow)" />
    <path d="M200 260 A 90 90 0 0 0 278 215" fill="none" stroke="#7fe0c0" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 4" />
    <defs><marker id="bd-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="6" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 Z" fill="#fff" /></marker></defs>
    <g font-family="Archivo Variable, Archivo, system-ui, sans-serif">
      <text x="200" y="30" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" font-weight="800" fill="#ff8fca">N</text>
      <text x="200" y="320" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#8c93c9">S</text>
      <circle cx="200" cy="170" r="13" fill="#fff" stroke="#c4157a" stroke-width="4" /><text x="200" y="175" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#161b3d">A</text>
      <circle cx="308" cy="232" r="13" fill="#fff" stroke="#c4157a" stroke-width="4" /><text x="308" y="237" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#161b3d">B</text>
      <text x="262" y="122" font-size="16" font-weight="800" fill="#fff">120°</text>
      <text x="246" y="282" font-size="13" fill="#7fe0c0">60°</text>
      <text x="400" y="80" font-size="15" fill="#aab0dc">Bearing (azimuth):</text>
      <text x="400" y="108" font-size="22" font-weight="800" fill="#fff">120°, clockwise from north</text>
      <text x="400" y="160" font-size="15" fill="#aab0dc">Quadrant bearing:</text>
      <text x="400" y="188" font-size="22" font-weight="800" fill="#7fe0c0">S 60° E</text>
      <text x="400" y="240" font-size="15" fill="#aab0dc">Back bearing, B to A:</text>
      <text x="400" y="268" font-size="22" font-weight="800" fill="#fff">300°, or N 60° W</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>A bearing is the angle from north, turning clockwise, to the direction of travel. Surveyors write the same direction as an angle east or west of north or south.</figcaption>
</figure>
